## Deploying to AWS (SST)

Follow the steps in order, from the repository root. Nothing reaches AWS before step 4.

### 1. Install the dependencies

```bash
{{> github-actions/package-manager}} install
```

### 2. Set the credentials and the region

{{> aws/credentials}}

SST deploys to `us-east-1` when no region is set. `AWS_PROFILE` takes precedence over a `profile` written in `sst.config.ts`, so leave the profile out of that file.

### 3. Install the SST providers

```bash
{{installedBinaryRunner}} sst install
```

This downloads the SST platform and writes `.sst/platform/config.d.ts`; it deploys nothing. `sst.config.ts` relies on the `$config` global that file declares, so `tsc` run at the root fails with `Cannot find name '$config'` (and the editor shows the same error) until `sst install` has run. `sst dev` and `sst deploy` run it themselves.

### 4. Optional: develop against AWS

```bash
{{installedBinaryRunner}} sst dev
```

This deploys your personal stage and runs the Lambda handlers from your machine against it, until you stop it. The first `sst dev` or `sst deploy` in an AWS account and region also bootstraps SST there, once (S3 buckets, an ECR repository and an SSM parameter).

### 5. Deploy

{{#if (projectSecrets "nextjs" "hono" "tanstack-start")}}
Set each runtime secret for the stage first; a deploy fails until they exist:

```bash
{{#each (projectSecrets "nextjs" "hono" "tanstack-start")}}
{{installedBinaryRunner}} sst secret set {{pascalCase this}} <value> --stage staging
{{/each}}
```

{{/if}}
```bash
{{installedBinaryRunner}} sst deploy --stage staging
```

`staging` is the stage the workflow deploys on a push to `main`; use `production` for the production stage. `sst deploy` prints the URL of each app and writes the same values to `.sst/outputs.json`. Remove a stage with `{{installedBinaryRunner}} sst remove --stage staging`.

### 6. Check the live URL

{{#if (eq blueprint "lambda-sst-hono")}}
```bash
API_URL=$(node -p "require('./.sst/outputs.json').api")
curl "${API_URL%/}/health/ping"
```

The answer is `{"ok":true,"message":"Health check","data":{"id":"ping"}}`.
{{else}}
Open the URL `sst deploy` printed for each app, or read them with `cat .sst/outputs.json`.
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq blueprint "lambda-sst-hono")}}

### 7. Deploy from GitHub Actions

On a push to `main` the workflow deploys the `staging` stage; a manual run deploys `staging` or `production`. The GitHub environments are named after the stages.

{{> aws/github-oidc environments="staging production"}}
{{/if}}
